; ted-findtoke-empty-list (#359): without a token list (TED alone,
; tokens = 0) findtoke walks a "node" at address 0.  Normally the long
; word at address 0 is 0 and the walk ends with "?????" - the result of
; the fix as well; inject nullnode makes it point to a token node (number
; $1234, name NULLNODE) while TED runs, as a non-zero long word there would.
; Lines "a", token $9234, "b", "c"; Block Save of lines 1-3 (the middle
; line goes through detoka5 -> findtoke, see #354).  Correct: findtoke
; does not look at address 0 (no NULLNODE in the file); the original
; follows the pointer at address 0 and writes NULLNODE.  Fixed in TED-C:
; findtoke and tokit know no token without a token list, and Block Save
; no longer detokenises without tokenise (#354).
; @fixed #359
; @file bo.bas "a\n\x92\x34\nb\nc"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject nullnode=1234/NULLNODE blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect file blk.txt "a\n"
; @expect nofile blk.txt "NULLNODE"
timeout 10
wait screen
key 50
menu 2 1
key 51
menu 1 2
wait freq "Name to save block as"
freq ok "TEDRUN:work/blk.txt"
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
